From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:43:40 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] regress: accept huff0 in the multiplex conninfo compression
 test

Fork-specific. With Compression yes both ends negotiate huff0@hpnssh.org,
not zlib, so "ssh -O conninfo" reports "compression huff0@hpnssh.org" and
regress/multiplex.sh failed at "cmd conninfo compression". The test now
accepts either name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 regress/multiplex.sh | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/regress/multiplex.sh b/regress/multiplex.sh
index e23f7d2b3..3e3bf049f 100644
--- a/regress/multiplex.sh
+++ b/regress/multiplex.sh
@@ -222,7 +222,7 @@ else
 fi
 if [ "$compression" = "yes" ]; then
 	verbose "test $tid: cmd conninfo compression"
-	if echo "$conninfo" | grep "compression zlib" >/dev/null &&
+	if echo "$conninfo" | grep -E "compression (zlib|huff0@hpnssh.org)" >/dev/null &&
 	    echo "$conninfo" | grep "compressed" >/dev/null; then
 		trace "ok conninfo compression"
 	else
